# Binary files, declared rather than guessed.
#
# core.autocrlf is true on the machines this repo is worked on, so git offers
# to rewrite line endings in everything it believes is text. It currently
# skips these only because its heuristic spots NUL bytes early in the file --
# which is a guess, not a rule. Committing a PDF already produced the
# "LF will be replaced by CRLF" warning, and a file that happened to have no
# NUL byte near the start would be silently rewritten and ruined on checkout.
# The bearing catalogue is 5.5 MB of spreadsheet and is not reproducible from
# anything in this repository.

*.pdf      binary
*.xlsx     binary
*.xls      binary
*.png      binary
*.jpg      binary
*.jpeg     binary
*.gif      binary
*.ico      binary
*.webp     binary
*.zip      binary
*.woff     binary
*.woff2    binary
*.ttf      binary
*.otf      binary
*.sqlite   binary
*.db       binary
